# Ashmedai

## Lore

The Crawling Horrors. Many are the fearsome stories about the Ashmedai, the monstrous servants of the Nightlords: that they live in some hellish dimension until summoned, that they are Nightbane and their worm-like forms are a Nightbane True Shape, or that they once guarded the mythical Formless Ones before switching allegiance when the Ba''al conquered the Nightlands.

As an independent race they have more initiative and self-reliance than the servile Hounds and Hunters, and the Nightlords use them on special missions. A few have left the service of the Ba''al - their malevolence makes any lasting alliance impossible - and roam the Waste or hunt humans for pleasure on Earth, where nests of up to six are rumored in some cities. The Nightlords persecute these renegades for their treachery and because they endanger the secrecy of the invasion.

The true form of an Ashmedai is a worm-like, fleshy giant with no apparent eyes, four long tentacles and a gaping maw filled with sharp teeth. But the creatures are master shape-shifters and can hide in human or animal shape, undetected and unsuspected; only some spells, psychic powers and Nightbane Talents can unmask them. They also have limited psionic powers that suit them to spying and manipulation. They have no Nightbane Talents, though some pass themselves off as Nightbane using rare artifacts made by the Nightlords.

A race of supernatural predators, the Ashmedai live on the life force of their victims rather than their flesh. They bite and tear, but rarely eat; the brutality flavors the life energies with terror and agony. Their shape-shifting makes them ideal agents for espionage and assassination. Some have joined the NSB, masquerading as Federal agents; others serve as bodyguards, enforcers and even political leaders.

## GM Notes

Average life span is believed to be 300 years, though some have lived much longer. As NPCs they are level 1D6+1, equivalent to a Psychic.

Alliances and allies: as servants of the Nightlords they often work alongside Hounds, Hunters and Hollow Men. The occasional renegade forms a temporary partnership with a vampire, a murderous human, or another supernatural menace.

Equipment: NSB agents are assigned Beretta 95 machine pistols (2D6, 20-round magazine, bursts and full automatic), or heavier weapons (M-16 rifles typically) if the situation demands it, and hazardous duty battle armor (A.R. 16, 260 S.D.C.).

Nightbanes'' Skins: a few elite agents are given these ancient artifacts - silky, light black capes absorbed into the skin until the wearer removes them. While worn, the wearer reads as Nightbane to other Nightbane, to detection spells and to psionic powers, but is drained of all P.P.E. until the Skin is removed (P.P.E. then recovers normally). A human or a vampire wearing one would also register as Nightbane. Fewer than 20 are known to exist, all in the possession of High King Moloch or his agents.
